&lt;td style="width: 124.85pt; border-top: 4.5pt solid #000000; border-right: 0.75pt solid #000000; border-bottom: 4.5pt solid #000000; padding-right: 4.72pt; padding-left: 6.4pt; vertical-align: bottom;"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: right; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;6,095&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;

&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 72pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;(1)&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Assets recoverable without earning a return.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-style: italic;"&gt;State income tax related. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Amounts represent the anticipated recovery from ratepayers of deferred state income taxes as a result of an increase in the Illinois state income tax rate from 7.75% to 9.5% effective July 1, 2017.These amounts are amortized to Account 410.1 &amp;#8220;Provision of Deferred Income Taxes&amp;#8221; over the remaining depreciable lives of the assets to which they apply. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-style: italic;"&gt;Federal income tax related. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Amounts represent the anticipated return to ratepayers of deferred income taxes as a result of the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act of 2017, which lowered the U.S. federal corporate income tax rate from 35% to 21% effective January 1, 2018. These amounts are amortized to Account 411.1 &amp;#8220;Provision for Deferred Income Taxes &amp;#8211; Credit&amp;#8221; over the remaining depreciable lives of the assets to which they apply.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-style: italic;"&gt;Deferred penalty revenues. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Amounts represent penalties collected from customers related to unauthorized overrun, balancing, and other services, which are refunded to non-offending shippers annually.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-style: italic;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;8. Commitments&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
